# S12-T06: Agent Auto-Registration in Presence

## App-agent preflight

- [ ] `explain("work-control")` — gates + agent activity
- [ ] Read `server/agents/run.ts` — task run state machine
- [ ] Read `server/utils/presence.ts` (T02) — joinRoom / leaveRoom API

## Implementation

When an agent task starts running, it MUST appear in the board-room presence
for the duration of the run (S12-INVARIANTS §5).

Modify `server/agents/run.ts` (or `run.post.ts` caller):

```ts
// Before status → in_progress:
const boardRoom = `board:${task.boardId}`
const agentMember: PresenceMember = {
  id: `agent:${task.id}`,
  kind: 'agent',
  role: task.leadRole ?? 'PM',
  label: task.leadRole ?? 'Agent'
}
joinRoom(boardRoom, agentMember)

// ... run task steps ...

// After status → done (or on error):
leaveRoom(boardRoom, `agent:${task.id}`)
broadcastPresence([boardRoom])
```

Add `broadcastPresence(rooms: string[])` helper to `presence.ts`:
```ts
export function broadcastPresence(rooms: string[]): void {
  for (const room of rooms) {
    const members = getRoomMembers(room)
    const { scopeType, scopeId } = roomToScope(room)
    broadcast({ type: 'presence.sync', scopeType, scopeId, members })
  }
}
```

Also add 30-second safety timeout: if agent crashes, presence is cleared.

## Done when

- [ ] Run a task → agent avatar appears in board presence during execution
- [ ] Task reaches `done` → agent avatar disappears within 1 s
- [ ] `bun run test` — run.ts unit test verifies joinRoom/leaveRoom called
